1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,044
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,128 --> 00:00:07,132
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,508 --> 00:00:10,677
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:12,762
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,846 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:17,892
[Ibyang] Aunt Audrey?

7
00:00:17,976 --> 00:00:18,810
[gasps]

8
00:00:18,893 --> 00:00:21,020
[Ibyang] Your lips look red.

9
00:00:21,104 --> 00:00:23,857
And Aunt Audrey's lipstick is fading.

10
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:24,941
Come on!

11
00:00:25,024 --> 00:00:25,984
Let's eat. Come on.

12
00:00:26,067 --> 00:00:30,405
[Noel] <i>My buddy thinks</i>
<i>Delfin stole you from me!</i>

13
00:00:31,156 --> 00:00:32,490
It's true, isn't it?!

14
00:00:32,574 --> 00:00:33,950
How many times did you do it, huh?!

15
00:00:34,034 --> 00:00:35,410
- [Cita] <i>You're hurting me.</i>
- [Noel] <i>How many times?!</i>

16
00:00:35,493 --> 00:00:37,954
Did something happen
between you and Aunt Audrey?

17
00:00:38,038 --> 00:00:39,789
[in English] Anyway,
it's-- It's complicated.

18
00:00:39,873 --> 00:00:40,957
[in English] It's complicated.

19
00:00:41,041 --> 00:00:42,667
[Red] <i>I'm still not comfortable</i>
<i>with that Atoy.</i>

20
00:00:42,751 --> 00:00:45,420
Audrey shouldn't have agreed
to co-parent with him.

21
00:00:46,045 --> 00:00:47,297
We can't do anything about it, hon.

22
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:48,923
[Red] <i>What if they get back together?</i>

23
00:00:49,007 --> 00:00:50,175
<i>What if they get married?</i>

24
00:00:50,258 --> 00:00:53,803
<i>If those two end up together,</i>
<i>it's like letting a snake into this house.</i>

25
00:00:53,887 --> 00:00:56,723
Is there a man with you inside the room?

26
00:00:56,806 --> 00:00:58,183
None, Dad.

27
00:00:58,266 --> 00:00:59,893
[in English] Uh,
I'll call you back later. Okay? Bye!

28
00:00:59,976 --> 00:01:02,395
You can't sit here. Find another table.

29
00:01:02,479 --> 00:01:05,231
[chair scraping, utensils shattering]

30
00:01:05,315 --> 00:01:08,985
A girl pulled her seat,
that's why she fell.

31
00:01:09,069 --> 00:01:10,195
[Janine] What's that?

32
00:01:10,278 --> 00:01:11,654
[Ibyang] <i>This really belongs</i>
<i>to Sister Tonet.</i>

33
00:01:11,738 --> 00:01:15,909
<i>I just borrowed it,</i>
<i>so I can always be with her.</i>

34
00:01:15,992 --> 00:01:17,786
[Audrey] <i>Janine is still upset with you.</i>

35
00:01:17,869 --> 00:01:20,538
I don't know how we'll tell her.

36
00:01:20,622 --> 00:01:22,457
PREVIOUSLY

37
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:24,125
[suave music playing]

38
00:01:24,209 --> 00:01:25,794
- [thuds softly]
- [groans]

39
00:01:25,877 --> 00:01:26,711
Ouchy.

40
00:01:26,795 --> 00:01:28,505
[hissing]

41
00:01:28,588 --> 00:01:30,173
[screams]

42
00:01:30,256 --> 00:01:31,674
[staff] There!

43
00:01:31,758 --> 00:01:33,051
So, you're here.

44
00:01:33,134 --> 00:01:34,803
Ma'am, are you ready for fishing?

45
00:01:34,886 --> 00:01:37,138
Uh, wait a moment.
Let's wait for the kids first.

46
00:01:37,222 --> 00:01:38,223
Ah, okay.

47
00:01:38,306 --> 00:01:40,016
- They're taking too long.
- Yes, they are.

48
00:01:40,517 --> 00:01:44,896
Ma'am, sir, the girl with you, Ibyang…

49
00:01:44,979 --> 00:01:47,065
She's at the lobby drinking water.

50
00:01:47,148 --> 00:01:48,900
She said she got lost
in the forest earlier.

51
00:01:48,983 --> 00:01:50,360
- [Audrey] What?
- Forest?

52
00:01:51,277 --> 00:01:52,195
What about Janine?

53
00:01:52,278 --> 00:01:54,280
What about her companion, the other girl?

54
00:01:54,364 --> 00:01:57,575
She said Janine took her
to the tall grass area,

55
00:01:57,659 --> 00:01:58,910
then left her there.

56
00:01:59,577 --> 00:02:02,205
She doesn't know
where her companion is now.

57
00:02:02,288 --> 00:02:04,541
Oh, no! Why did they go there?

58
00:02:04,624 --> 00:02:06,459
There are monitor lizards
and snakes there.

59
00:02:06,543 --> 00:02:07,919
- Especially now, it's summer.
- My God.

60
00:02:08,002 --> 00:02:09,462
- Please come with us there.
- [Atoy] Let's go, let's go.

61
00:02:09,546 --> 00:02:10,672
- Ah, let's find Janine.
- [indistinct]

62
00:02:10,755 --> 00:02:12,173
- Come on, Atoy!
- [Atoy] Where?

63
00:02:13,550 --> 00:02:14,968
[suave theme music playing]

64
00:02:15,051 --> 00:02:16,886
[motorcycle revving]

65
00:02:16,970 --> 00:02:18,805
[sewing machine whirring]

66
00:02:18,888 --> 00:02:21,349
[snipping]

67
00:02:21,432 --> 00:02:24,686
[sewing machine clacking]

68
00:02:24,769 --> 00:02:26,229
- [gun cocks]
- [gunfire]

69
00:02:26,312 --> 00:02:28,064
[gunfire]

70
00:02:28,148 --> 00:02:30,358
[clicking]

71
00:02:30,441 --> 00:02:32,443
[snipping]

72
00:02:32,527 --> 00:02:34,571
[music swells]

73
00:02:34,654 --> 00:02:38,408
[electronic blipping]

74
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:45,081
[Cita] Karla.

75
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:47,375
[sighs]

76
00:02:47,458 --> 00:02:49,335
Just be patient with your father, okay.

77
00:02:50,003 --> 00:02:52,338
Next time, I'll set aside food for you.

78
00:02:54,841 --> 00:02:56,551
It's fine, Mom. I'm okay here.

79
00:02:56,634 --> 00:02:58,970
Even if the food at home is delicious,

80
00:02:59,053 --> 00:03:01,973
it tastes bad when you eat
with someone negative.

81
00:03:02,891 --> 00:03:05,685
Maybe your father just woke up
on the wrong side of the bed.

82
00:03:05,768 --> 00:03:08,438
Where's Ame?

83
00:03:08,521 --> 00:03:09,606
She bought something outside.

84
00:03:11,774 --> 00:03:12,859
[sighs]

85
00:03:17,864 --> 00:03:19,449
[suspicious music playing]

86
00:03:19,532 --> 00:03:20,742
Mom, what's this?

87
00:03:23,453 --> 00:03:27,540
Ah-- Dirt. Maybe I walked
through some dirt earlier.

88
00:03:28,166 --> 00:03:29,125
That's a bruise, isn't it?

89
00:03:30,418 --> 00:03:33,379
Where did you get this?
You never got that before.

90
00:03:36,883 --> 00:03:37,884
Dad?

91
00:03:39,302 --> 00:03:42,722
[tense music playing]

92
00:03:42,805 --> 00:03:43,848
Karla!

93
00:03:44,766 --> 00:03:46,226
- Karla!
- [Audrey] Janine!

94
00:03:46,309 --> 00:03:47,560
- [Audrey] Oh my God!
- [Atoy] Janine!

95
00:03:47,644 --> 00:03:49,562
- [Audrey] Ja-Janine, my dear!
- [Atoy] Janine.

96
00:03:49,646 --> 00:03:50,688
[Audrey gasping]

97
00:03:50,772 --> 00:03:51,606
[staff] Wait, wait.

98
00:03:51,689 --> 00:03:53,233
[ominous music playing]

99
00:03:53,316 --> 00:03:55,193
[gasps] My child!

100
00:03:55,860 --> 00:03:58,529
[Atoy] Her heartbeat is fast, and there's…

101
00:03:58,613 --> 00:04:00,490
- [Audrey gasping]
- [Atoy, in English] Snakebite.

102
00:04:01,491 --> 00:04:02,951
She was bitten by a snake.

103
00:04:03,034 --> 00:04:04,786
Oh, no! Oh, child!

104
00:04:04,869 --> 00:04:05,954
[music swells]

105
00:04:06,037 --> 00:04:09,040
Help us. Help her!

106
00:04:09,123 --> 00:04:10,124
[Atoy] Let's go.

107
00:04:10,208 --> 00:04:12,001
[Audrey] Janine, my child!

108
00:04:12,085 --> 00:04:14,545
Dad! Dad!

109
00:04:14,629 --> 00:04:17,715
Karla, don't fight
with your father anymore.

110
00:04:18,675 --> 00:04:20,510
Admit it to me first.

111
00:04:20,593 --> 00:04:21,594
Did he hurt you?

112
00:04:21,678 --> 00:04:23,179
Here, look!

113
00:04:23,972 --> 00:04:25,056
What's this?

114
00:04:27,225 --> 00:04:29,352
It's my fault.

115
00:04:30,144 --> 00:04:33,231
We fought. I disrespected him.

116
00:04:33,314 --> 00:04:35,608
That's normal for married couples.

117
00:04:36,150 --> 00:04:38,111
Mom, it's normal to fight.

118
00:04:38,611 --> 00:04:40,530
But it's not normal for him to hurt you,

119
00:04:40,613 --> 00:04:42,490
especially when you're fighting.

120
00:04:42,991 --> 00:04:45,118
Especially since you're his wife!

121
00:04:45,201 --> 00:04:47,203
[pensive music playing]

122
00:04:47,287 --> 00:04:49,163
It won't happen again.

123
00:04:49,247 --> 00:04:51,708
Mom, you don't know that!

124
00:04:53,001 --> 00:04:54,836
Mom, it's 2026.

125
00:04:54,919 --> 00:04:57,463
You don't have to put up with that man.

126
00:04:57,547 --> 00:05:01,259
It's obvious you don't love him,
and he hurts you.

127
00:05:01,342 --> 00:05:03,678
He's a drunkard and a gambler.

128
00:05:04,637 --> 00:05:06,681
Mom, he has no redeeming qualities.

129
00:05:06,764 --> 00:05:08,391
Kick him out.

130
00:05:08,474 --> 00:05:10,768
Karla, he's still your father.

131
00:05:10,852 --> 00:05:13,187
Mom, I always hear that.

132
00:05:14,105 --> 00:05:16,357
That mindset is toxic.

133
00:05:16,441 --> 00:05:17,942
Just because he's my father doesn't mean

134
00:05:18,026 --> 00:05:21,195
he automatically has immunity
from all his sins.

135
00:05:21,279 --> 00:05:22,822
No way.

136
00:05:24,449 --> 00:05:26,659
It's my fault anyway.

137
00:05:27,368 --> 00:05:30,872
Karla, don't you love your father anymore?

138
00:05:31,497 --> 00:05:34,125
Mom, I have no choice but to love him.

139
00:05:34,792 --> 00:05:36,669
I grew up knowing he was my father.

140
00:05:38,337 --> 00:05:40,715
But he was never a dad to me.

141
00:05:41,799 --> 00:05:44,010
Mom, he's not a loss in my life.

142
00:05:44,093 --> 00:05:45,261
[Cita sniffles]

143
00:05:45,762 --> 00:05:48,181
So, if you can't kick him out,

144
00:05:48,973 --> 00:05:49,974
I will.

145
00:05:50,058 --> 00:05:55,188
[rousing music playing]

146
00:05:58,149 --> 00:06:00,902
[doctor] Good thing the snake
was non-venomous.

147
00:06:01,527 --> 00:06:05,323
We already administered
an anti-tetanus booster for the snakebite.

148
00:06:05,865 --> 00:06:07,825
She had symptoms of heatstroke,

149
00:06:07,909 --> 00:06:10,536
which is why she was found unconscious.

150
00:06:11,079 --> 00:06:15,750
She already has an ice pack
and IV fluids for hydration.

151
00:06:15,833 --> 00:06:17,418
We continue to monitor the patient,

152
00:06:17,502 --> 00:06:21,798
but most likely, your child
will be discharged tonight.

153
00:06:22,381 --> 00:06:23,800
[Audrey] Thank you.

154
00:06:23,883 --> 00:06:24,926
[in English] Thank you, Doc.

155
00:06:25,510 --> 00:06:26,427
[Atoy] Oh.

156
00:06:28,221 --> 00:06:29,847
Your daughter is okay now.

157
00:06:29,931 --> 00:06:31,057
Um…

158
00:06:31,140 --> 00:06:32,975
Good thing we found her right away.

159
00:06:33,059 --> 00:06:34,268
Because otherwise,

160
00:06:34,352 --> 00:06:38,773
her other organs might have shut down
because of the heatstroke.

161
00:06:38,856 --> 00:06:42,819
What if the snake had been venomous?

162
00:06:42,902 --> 00:06:45,738
Why are you thinking that?
It wasn't venomous, come on.

163
00:06:46,489 --> 00:06:49,200
I shouldn't have left her with Ibyang.

164
00:06:50,618 --> 00:06:51,744
Oh?

165
00:06:51,828 --> 00:06:52,912
Wait.

166
00:06:52,995 --> 00:06:55,414
Wait. Are you saying
this is Ibyang's fault?

167
00:06:56,415 --> 00:06:58,835
I know it's not her fault.

168
00:06:59,794 --> 00:07:01,504
But it's true.

169
00:07:01,587 --> 00:07:03,381
This wouldn't have happened
to our daughter

170
00:07:03,464 --> 00:07:04,924
if Ibyang wasn't there!

171
00:07:05,007 --> 00:07:06,843
I know Ibyang.

172
00:07:06,926 --> 00:07:08,261
She's not a bad kid.

173
00:07:08,344 --> 00:07:09,971
She wouldn't do that.

174
00:07:10,513 --> 00:07:12,181
So, what are you saying?

175
00:07:12,265 --> 00:07:13,808
That our daughter is bad?

176
00:07:14,559 --> 00:07:17,019
What kind of father are you to think that?

177
00:07:18,146 --> 00:07:20,314
[in English] Janine may not
be perfect, Atoy.

178
00:07:20,940 --> 00:07:23,860
But maybe you're forgetting
she's your child.

179
00:07:23,943 --> 00:07:29,031
[rousing music playing]

180
00:07:30,616 --> 00:07:32,034
Janine, my child.

181
00:07:43,129 --> 00:07:45,256
[Janine] I accompanied her
to the restroom,

182
00:07:45,339 --> 00:07:48,259
but she said she wanted to go somewhere,

183
00:07:48,342 --> 00:07:49,927
beyond the fence.

184
00:07:50,970 --> 00:07:53,681
We went because she said

185
00:07:54,182 --> 00:07:56,350
there was a beautiful view there.

186
00:07:56,434 --> 00:08:00,521
Then, when I looked back,
she suddenly disappeared.

187
00:08:00,605 --> 00:08:02,565
[pensive music playing]

188
00:08:02,648 --> 00:08:04,942
She deliberately made me get lost.

189
00:08:05,526 --> 00:08:07,361
Was that really her intention?

190
00:08:08,029 --> 00:08:09,906
Janine, think carefully.

191
00:08:09,989 --> 00:08:12,200
[pensive music playing]

192
00:08:12,283 --> 00:08:13,868
Is that really what happened?

193
00:08:14,744 --> 00:08:15,828
[Janine] Yes, Daddy.

194
00:08:16,662 --> 00:08:18,831
Don't you believe me?

195
00:08:18,915 --> 00:08:22,710
[suspicious music playing]

196
00:08:23,294 --> 00:08:26,380
Did Ibyang tell you another story,
that's why

197
00:08:26,881 --> 00:08:28,216
you believe her instead?

198
00:08:28,299 --> 00:08:29,800
Is that it, huh?

199
00:08:29,884 --> 00:08:31,135
[sniffles]

200
00:08:32,136 --> 00:08:34,430
Why-- Why do you always side with her?

201
00:08:35,473 --> 00:08:38,643
You know, I feel like
I'm not your child because…

202
00:08:38,726 --> 00:08:41,145
it seems you love Ibyang more than me.

203
00:08:41,229 --> 00:08:44,065
Janine, don't say that. That's not true.

204
00:08:44,690 --> 00:08:46,234
Of course, we love you both.

205
00:08:46,317 --> 00:08:49,654
- Ah, let's--
- Ah, Atoy, can we talk outside?

206
00:08:50,738 --> 00:08:55,910
[pensive music playing]

207
00:09:08,297 --> 00:09:10,424
- [Siony] There are no women's clothes.
- [Karla] Ten pesos, one garment!

208
00:09:10,508 --> 00:09:11,884
- Oh, just ten!-
- [indistinct]

209
00:09:11,968 --> 00:09:13,386
- I'll take some
- Just ten pesos,

210
00:09:13,469 --> 00:09:14,595
- for my nephew.
- one garment!

211
00:09:14,679 --> 00:09:15,972
This suits you, yes.

212
00:09:16,055 --> 00:09:17,515
- [woman] Oh, here, shoes!
- [indistinct]

213
00:09:17,598 --> 00:09:19,016
- That fits you, yes.
- [indistinct]

214
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:21,519
- This too, it looks good on you.
- Oh, right, Mom! That's fine, oh!

215
00:09:21,602 --> 00:09:22,812
- [Karla] Yes, only ten pesos.
- Oh, this.

216
00:09:22,895 --> 00:09:23,896
- [Noel] Hey, hey!
- [indistinct]

217
00:09:23,980 --> 00:09:24,939
Hey, move!

218
00:09:25,022 --> 00:09:26,274
[ominous music playing]

219
00:09:26,357 --> 00:09:28,359
These are mine! These are my clothes!

220
00:09:29,193 --> 00:09:30,111
They're not for sale!

221
00:09:31,404 --> 00:09:34,156
- We already paid for some of them.
- You'll regret this, Karla!

222
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:35,449
Don't worry!

223
00:09:35,533 --> 00:09:38,911
Everything I sell here,
I'll give to you, so you can leave!

224
00:09:38,995 --> 00:09:41,163
You're kicking me out, you rude child?!

225
00:09:42,290 --> 00:09:44,041
You're not?!

226
00:09:44,750 --> 00:09:47,003
My mother is so kind to you.

227
00:09:47,086 --> 00:09:49,297
She served you more than me,

228
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:51,299
and you still hurt her!

229
00:09:51,382 --> 00:09:54,093
My mother will not be
a battered wife as long as I live.

230
00:09:54,176 --> 00:09:55,886
So, get out!

231
00:09:55,970 --> 00:09:57,847
Oh, Noel!

232
00:09:57,930 --> 00:09:59,724
You're beating up Cita?!

233
00:09:59,807 --> 00:10:02,184
[gasps] You're so cruel!

234
00:10:02,268 --> 00:10:03,686
You're such a bad person!

235
00:10:03,769 --> 00:10:05,229
- Yes! That's forbidden, right?
- [clamoring]

236
00:10:05,313 --> 00:10:07,189
- [clamoring]
- [tense music playing]

237
00:10:07,273 --> 00:10:10,359
You're all gossipmongers!

238
00:10:10,443 --> 00:10:12,028
Get out!

239
00:10:12,612 --> 00:10:14,572
- Out! So early--
- Your clothes are ugly anyway!

240
00:10:14,655 --> 00:10:16,157
You're uglier!

241
00:10:16,240 --> 00:10:17,867
- [cackles]
- [clamoring]

242
00:10:17,950 --> 00:10:19,827
Get out! You're all ugly!

243
00:10:19,910 --> 00:10:21,329
[Siony] Stop drinking!

244
00:10:21,412 --> 00:10:23,623
You're ruining the day!

245
00:10:23,706 --> 00:10:24,915
Out!

246
00:10:24,999 --> 00:10:26,000
- We're right here!
- Out!

247
00:10:26,083 --> 00:10:28,377
- We're right here, Karla!
- You can't enter our house!

248
00:10:28,461 --> 00:10:29,837
This is my home!

249
00:10:30,463 --> 00:10:31,631
- [grunts]
- Noel, Noel!

250
00:10:31,714 --> 00:10:32,715
- No way!
- [Noel] What?!

251
00:10:32,798 --> 00:10:35,384
I'm just making sure
she's telling the truth.

252
00:10:35,468 --> 00:10:39,847
Maybe you're forgetting
that this child has a tendency to lie.

253
00:10:39,930 --> 00:10:41,015
What?

254
00:10:41,515 --> 00:10:44,352
Janine already cried to you,
and that's what you're thinking?!

255
00:10:44,435 --> 00:10:46,145
Listen first.

256
00:10:47,897 --> 00:10:51,776
At the restaurant,
didn't Ibyang fall from the chair?

257
00:10:52,818 --> 00:10:55,279
Oh, I talked to a kid.

258
00:10:55,363 --> 00:10:59,992
She said Janine really pulled
the chair, that's why Ibyang fell.

259
00:11:00,076 --> 00:11:03,746
Oh? I didn't tell you, so there wouldn't
be trouble because I don't want trouble.

260
00:11:03,829 --> 00:11:05,581
- I want us to enjoy.
- [in English] You know what? Okay, fine.

261
00:11:06,207 --> 00:11:07,875
So, Ibyang fell from the chair.

262
00:11:08,542 --> 00:11:09,877
Maybe she already suffered for it,

263
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:13,756
since our daughter was bitten
by a snake and had heatstroke!

264
00:11:13,839 --> 00:11:15,132
Suffered?

265
00:11:15,633 --> 00:11:16,759
[in English] Oh, wait.

266
00:11:17,635 --> 00:11:19,595
I'm not happy about what happened, okay.

267
00:11:19,678 --> 00:11:24,392
What I'm saying is, I don't want
this child to get used to lying.

268
00:11:24,475 --> 00:11:26,060
She always makes up stories.

269
00:11:26,143 --> 00:11:27,770
Poor Ibyang!

270
00:11:27,853 --> 00:11:29,814
[pensive music playing]

271
00:11:29,897 --> 00:11:32,274
Our daughter deserves pity too.

272
00:11:37,196 --> 00:11:39,448
[nurse] Ma'am, your child is calling you.

273
00:11:41,283 --> 00:11:47,415
- [sinister music playing]
- [phone ringing]

274
00:11:48,165 --> 00:11:50,251
- Hello?
- [Gemma] <i>Hello, Sir Atoy?</i>

275
00:11:50,334 --> 00:11:52,545
<i>Ibyang and I are here at the hospital.</i>

276
00:11:52,628 --> 00:11:54,505
<i>She wants to see Janine.</i>

277
00:11:54,588 --> 00:11:58,259
Yes, okay. I'll go out
to the hallway near the ER.

278
00:11:58,342 --> 00:11:59,802
Let's meet there.

279
00:12:01,178 --> 00:12:03,806
You're unbelievable, Cita!

280
00:12:04,598 --> 00:12:07,977
Why did you let your child
put my things outside?!

281
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:12,273
If you want me to leave, you say it to me!

282
00:12:12,356 --> 00:12:14,400
Don't yell at my mother!

283
00:12:15,067 --> 00:12:17,361
Karla, don't butt in, okay!

284
00:12:17,445 --> 00:12:20,156
- This is between me and my wife!
- Karla, Karla!

285
00:12:20,239 --> 00:12:22,408
Let me and your father talk first.

286
00:12:22,491 --> 00:12:24,535
- Go on.
- No, Mom.

287
00:12:24,618 --> 00:12:27,872
I won't leave you
to your worthless husband!

288
00:12:28,539 --> 00:12:30,374
Repeat what you said!

289
00:12:30,458 --> 00:12:32,168
You're worthless!

290
00:12:32,251 --> 00:12:34,920
I wish you weren't the one my mom married!

291
00:12:35,004 --> 00:12:37,882
I'm okay with not being able
to live in this world,

292
00:12:37,965 --> 00:12:41,635
as long as you aren't
my mom's husband and she's happy!

293
00:12:41,719 --> 00:12:43,053
You imbecile!

294
00:12:43,137 --> 00:12:45,347
- Hey! Stop it! You know…
- What's the matter with you?!

295
00:12:45,431 --> 00:12:46,849
- You're so ungrateful!
- [Karla grunts]

296
00:12:46,932 --> 00:12:49,143
- Let her go!
- You're so ungrateful!

297
00:12:49,226 --> 00:12:50,186
Both of you should leave!

298
00:12:50,269 --> 00:12:51,437
- [Noel] You leave!
- [Cita] Let her go!

299
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:53,647
- I'll take my mother with me!
- [clamoring]

300
00:12:53,731 --> 00:12:54,982
[Karla] Mom!

301
00:12:55,065 --> 00:12:56,275
[grunts]

302
00:12:56,358 --> 00:12:58,360
[thuds, then clinks]

303
00:12:58,444 --> 00:13:00,029
Karla, stop!

304
00:13:00,112 --> 00:13:01,864
Karla, stop.

305
00:13:01,947 --> 00:13:03,782
[Cita cries] Stop, stop.

306
00:13:03,866 --> 00:13:09,455
[ominous music playing]

307
00:13:11,373 --> 00:13:12,583
- [grunts]
- [screams]

308
00:13:12,666 --> 00:13:13,918
[foreboding music playing]

309
00:13:14,001 --> 00:13:15,085
- [Noel] Get out of there!
- [Karla] Drop that!

310
00:13:15,169 --> 00:13:16,337
I'll kill her!

311
00:13:16,420 --> 00:13:17,338
[wails]

312
00:13:19,089 --> 00:13:20,049
Mom.

313
00:13:24,011 --> 00:13:26,388
[sobs] You're truly an animal.

314
00:13:26,472 --> 00:13:30,976
[sobbing] I'll kill you first
before you kill my child.

315
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:33,187
[tense music playing]

316
00:13:34,355 --> 00:13:36,607
[sobs] I put up with you.

317
00:13:36,690 --> 00:13:39,401
I took all the insults you threw at me

318
00:13:39,485 --> 00:13:41,362
and your resentment toward me.

319
00:13:41,445 --> 00:13:43,155
But for you to involve my child?

320
00:13:43,239 --> 00:13:44,573
[sobs] I won't allow it.

321
00:13:44,657 --> 00:13:46,992
[sobs] We're done.

322
00:13:47,076 --> 00:13:48,327
Leave!

323
00:13:48,410 --> 00:13:49,745
Cita.

324
00:13:50,454 --> 00:13:51,789
[thumps softly]

325
00:13:51,872 --> 00:13:54,166
Maybe you forgot!

326
00:13:54,667 --> 00:13:58,963
I saved you from shame!

327
00:13:59,630 --> 00:14:01,173
You should be thankful

328
00:14:01,882 --> 00:14:04,760
because I accepted your child,

329
00:14:04,843 --> 00:14:07,638
even though she's not mine!

330
00:14:07,721 --> 00:14:09,139
[rousing music playing]

331
00:14:09,223 --> 00:14:10,182
What?!

332
00:14:19,984 --> 00:14:23,904
[sobbing]

333
00:14:23,988 --> 00:14:24,864
Mom…

334
00:14:26,824 --> 00:14:28,617
What is he saying?

335
00:14:28,701 --> 00:14:31,287
Say that again. I'm not your daughter?

336
00:14:31,370 --> 00:14:34,039
What, Cita?

337
00:14:35,583 --> 00:14:37,334
Tell her the truth!

338
00:14:38,043 --> 00:14:42,882
So, she'll be embarrassed
for trying to kick me out!

339
00:14:42,965 --> 00:14:44,758
[sobs]

340
00:14:44,842 --> 00:14:47,219
I'm the one kicking you out-- [sobs]

341
00:14:47,303 --> 00:14:49,972
I don't want you anymore.

342
00:14:50,055 --> 00:14:51,181
[sobs]

343
00:14:51,891 --> 00:14:54,643
Because I hurt you, huh?!

344
00:14:54,727 --> 00:14:56,854
[pensive music playing]

345
00:14:56,937 --> 00:15:01,066
That's just right
because you cheated on me!

346
00:15:01,150 --> 00:15:03,360
You cheated on me!

347
00:15:03,444 --> 00:15:06,906
Mom, what is he saying?

348
00:15:06,989 --> 00:15:10,826
[sobbing]

349
00:15:10,910 --> 00:15:15,789
Cita, don't cry your way out of this!

350
00:15:16,582 --> 00:15:18,167
Tell the truth!

351
00:15:19,543 --> 00:15:23,631
I'm not the only bad spouse here.
You are too!

352
00:15:23,714 --> 00:15:24,715
Right?!

353
00:15:24,798 --> 00:15:27,176
Why don't you tell her the truth?!

354
00:15:28,135 --> 00:15:31,221
You can't, because it's shameful?!

355
00:15:32,264 --> 00:15:34,642
Because you're so ashamed?!

356
00:15:36,060 --> 00:15:37,770
Mom, tell me now, Mom.

357
00:15:37,853 --> 00:15:39,605
[sobbing]

358
00:15:39,688 --> 00:15:41,273
Who is my father, Mom?

359
00:15:41,357 --> 00:15:45,319
[sobbing]

360
00:15:45,402 --> 00:15:46,487
It's Delfin!

361
00:15:47,196 --> 00:15:48,948
Delfin is your father!

362
00:15:49,031 --> 00:15:51,075
Atoy is your brother!

363
00:15:51,158 --> 00:15:53,035
- [tense music playing]
- [sobbing]

364
00:15:53,118 --> 00:15:54,828
Mom, is that true?

365
00:15:55,746 --> 00:15:57,873
She won't admit it to you!

366
00:15:59,208 --> 00:16:02,044
Because her image will be ruined!

367
00:16:03,128 --> 00:16:06,006
But your mother cheated on me!

368
00:16:06,090 --> 00:16:07,007
She's promiscuous!

369
00:16:07,675 --> 00:16:09,051
Stop it!

370
00:16:09,134 --> 00:16:10,970
Stop it!

371
00:16:11,053 --> 00:16:13,681
All right now! Yes!

372
00:16:14,682 --> 00:16:16,642
[sobs] I made a mistake then!

373
00:16:16,725 --> 00:16:18,769
[sobs] But I don't want this anymore.

374
00:16:20,062 --> 00:16:22,231
I can't accept you anymore.
I don't want you.

375
00:16:22,314 --> 00:16:24,441
Get out of here!

376
00:16:24,525 --> 00:16:26,944
- Leave!
- [Karla] Mom!

377
00:16:27,027 --> 00:16:30,322
- You leave! You!
- That's enough!

378
00:16:30,406 --> 00:16:33,909
Even if she wronged you,
you have no right to hurt her!

379
00:16:34,994 --> 00:16:35,995
[sobs]

380
00:16:36,078 --> 00:16:39,081
Enough. Noel, that's enough.
That's enough.

381
00:16:39,164 --> 00:16:40,916
[sobbing]

382
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,042
Karla, that's enough.

383
00:16:42,126 --> 00:16:44,420
[sobbing]

384
00:16:44,503 --> 00:16:47,214
[in English] So, is Miss Cita
in danger right now?

385
00:16:47,297 --> 00:16:49,758
[in English] I mean, if her husband
is punching her, right?

386
00:16:49,842 --> 00:16:52,052
[in English] I think so! Cannot be!

387
00:16:52,136 --> 00:16:54,763
- [in English] Uh, the situation here is--
- [boy] Brother Nestor!

388
00:16:54,847 --> 00:16:56,306
- Oh, oh?
- Oh?

389
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:58,225
[in English] Soft drinks, soft drinks,
soft drinks. He wants--

390
00:16:58,308 --> 00:16:59,601
- No, no, no, no.
- [Nestor] What?

391
00:16:59,685 --> 00:17:01,395
There's a fight at Miss Cita's house!

392
00:17:01,478 --> 00:17:02,312
Huh?

393
00:17:02,396 --> 00:17:06,066
Then, Sir Noel is beating Karla!

394
00:17:06,150 --> 00:17:07,526
- Let's go!
- [Nestor] Huh?!

395
00:17:07,609 --> 00:17:08,944
- Let's go!
- [panicking]

396
00:17:09,528 --> 00:17:11,321
- Here, a stick!
- Here it is. Okay.

397
00:17:11,405 --> 00:17:13,615
- [sobs]
- Leave!

398
00:17:13,699 --> 00:17:14,783
Get out of here!

399
00:17:14,867 --> 00:17:16,410
- [Noel] Leave--
- [clamoring]

400
00:17:16,493 --> 00:17:17,786
- [Noel] Leave!
- [clamoring]

401
00:17:17,870 --> 00:17:19,163
Leave Cita alone!

402
00:17:19,246 --> 00:17:21,123
[in English] That's violence
against women!

403
00:17:21,206 --> 00:17:23,292
- Don't meddle!
- [Cita sobs]

404
00:17:23,375 --> 00:17:24,293
- Don't meddle.
- Go get him!

405
00:17:24,376 --> 00:17:25,294
Leave!

406
00:17:25,377 --> 00:17:27,963
- Arrest him!
- Don't meddle!

407
00:17:28,047 --> 00:17:28,881
[clamoring]

408
00:17:28,964 --> 00:17:30,049
- Don't meddle!
- [clamoring]

409
00:17:30,132 --> 00:17:31,717
- Get out of here!
- Come with us!

410
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:33,844
What?!

411
00:17:33,927 --> 00:17:35,387
[sobbing]

412
00:17:35,471 --> 00:17:36,472
Sit down first.

413
00:17:36,555 --> 00:17:38,891
[sobbing]

414
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:41,101
Are you okay, child?

415
00:17:41,185 --> 00:17:43,771
[sobbing]

416
00:17:44,354 --> 00:17:47,900
What happened to Janine isn't my fault.

417
00:17:50,319 --> 00:17:54,573
She took Sister Tonet's bag charm,
then threw it.

418
00:17:55,282 --> 00:17:57,367
Then she suddenly disappeared.

419
00:18:00,245 --> 00:18:04,583
[melancholic music playing]

420
00:18:04,666 --> 00:18:05,667
[Atoy] Okay.

421
00:18:07,753 --> 00:18:08,879
Why are you crying?

422
00:18:10,589 --> 00:18:14,218
Because… [sobs]

423
00:18:14,301 --> 00:18:17,054
Maybe you'll be mad at me.

424
00:18:17,888 --> 00:18:18,972
[sobs]

425
00:18:19,056 --> 00:18:23,018
I didn't want Janine
to get into an accident.

426
00:18:24,269 --> 00:18:31,026
Even if we fight,
I don't want her harmed, because…

427
00:18:31,860 --> 00:18:34,488
[sobs] you love her too.

428
00:18:37,866 --> 00:18:39,076
[sighs]

429
00:18:43,163 --> 00:18:44,164
Let's go.

430
00:18:49,837 --> 00:18:51,797
Aunt Audrey.

431
00:18:54,133 --> 00:18:56,510
Are you mad at me?

432
00:18:59,930 --> 00:19:01,557
No, Ibyang.

433
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:05,144
Atoy, your child is looking for you.

434
00:19:05,227 --> 00:19:06,603
I'll just bring her back to the resort.

435
00:19:06,687 --> 00:19:08,522
The staff who brought her
earlier already left.

436
00:19:08,605 --> 00:19:10,691
She can wait here.

437
00:19:10,774 --> 00:19:12,359
She can't stay here.
She's not allowed here.

438
00:19:12,442 --> 00:19:14,528
- I'll be quick--
- Atoy, what's wrong with you?!

439
00:19:14,611 --> 00:19:17,322
Your daughter is looking for you!
She's not your child!

440
00:19:17,406 --> 00:19:22,828
[intense music playing]

441
00:19:30,919 --> 00:19:33,130
[in English] I'm--
I'm so-- I'm so sorry, Ibyang.

442
00:19:34,214 --> 00:19:36,508
I-I didn't mean it.

443
00:19:37,217 --> 00:19:38,468
[Ibyang] It's true.

444
00:19:38,552 --> 00:19:40,762
[sobs]

445
00:19:40,846 --> 00:19:43,307
I'm not really your child.

446
00:19:45,017 --> 00:19:45,851
Ibyang…

447
00:19:47,644 --> 00:19:50,397
Um, just wait for me there, okay?

448
00:19:51,023 --> 00:19:51,940
Just wait for me.

449
00:19:52,566 --> 00:19:53,483
All right.

450
00:19:56,361 --> 00:19:57,237
What was that?

451
00:19:58,197 --> 00:19:59,198
Why did you say that?

452
00:19:59,281 --> 00:20:01,533
Why are you talking like that
in front of her?

453
00:20:01,617 --> 00:20:03,285
I didn't mean it.

454
00:20:04,077 --> 00:20:06,788
[in English] I have nothing
against Ibyang.

455
00:20:07,372 --> 00:20:09,208
But I'm frustrated with you!

456
00:20:10,459 --> 00:20:13,337
You tell me you want
our family to be whole,

457
00:20:13,420 --> 00:20:16,965
but you prioritize
another child over your own!

458
00:20:17,049 --> 00:20:19,426
What other child? She's not another child.

459
00:20:19,509 --> 00:20:21,053
Ibyang is my responsibility.

460
00:20:21,136 --> 00:20:23,013
I promised her I would take care of her.

461
00:20:23,096 --> 00:20:26,725
But what Janine wants
is just the three of us as a family.

462
00:20:26,808 --> 00:20:30,145
Look. I really do like Ibyang,

463
00:20:30,229 --> 00:20:34,316
but when the two are together,
it's always a disaster!

464
00:20:34,816 --> 00:20:37,319
[in English] They bring out the worst
in each other, Atoy.

465
00:20:37,402 --> 00:20:38,946
They really don't get along!

466
00:20:39,029 --> 00:20:41,406
No, it's just for now! They're kids.

467
00:20:41,490 --> 00:20:43,033
Look, when they grow up, they'll mature.

468
00:20:43,116 --> 00:20:45,661
They'll just laugh
about what they're doing now.

469
00:20:45,744 --> 00:20:47,079
[Audrey] No!

470
00:20:47,162 --> 00:20:49,581
[in English] It'll only get worse.

471
00:20:50,207 --> 00:20:54,169
You have to understand.
Janine grew up in an orphanage,

472
00:20:54,253 --> 00:20:57,339
where she carried
the feeling of being rejected.

473
00:20:57,422 --> 00:20:58,590
That's why she ended up there.

474
00:20:59,174 --> 00:21:02,552
Then, the first one who adopted her
didn't love her either.

475
00:21:02,636 --> 00:21:05,389
So, I understand
why she doesn't want to share us.

476
00:21:06,765 --> 00:21:09,142
Because as long as Ibyang is here,

477
00:21:09,226 --> 00:21:13,313
she'll always feel
she'll never be enough for us.

478
00:21:14,398 --> 00:21:18,235
Atoy, this isn't a shallow insecurity

479
00:21:18,318 --> 00:21:21,363
that will just disappear
when she grows up.

480
00:21:22,322 --> 00:21:25,534
This is a deep wound she still carries.

481
00:21:25,617 --> 00:21:31,039
[melodramatic music playing]

482
00:21:33,750 --> 00:21:35,794
So, what do you want me to do now?

483
00:21:39,172 --> 00:21:40,507
You must choose.

484
00:21:40,590 --> 00:21:42,009
[music fades]

485
00:21:42,092 --> 00:21:44,469
Your child or Ibyang?

486
00:21:45,137 --> 00:21:46,179
Son of--

487
00:21:46,847 --> 00:21:48,682
Don't-- Don't make me do that.

488
00:21:48,765 --> 00:21:49,975
You're unbelievable.

489
00:21:50,559 --> 00:21:51,685
[in English] I'm sorry.

490
00:21:52,352 --> 00:21:54,521
But you can only have one child.

491
00:21:55,981 --> 00:21:57,316
Janine…

492
00:21:59,026 --> 00:22:00,193
or Ibyang.

493
00:22:12,664 --> 00:22:14,207
This is crazy.

494
00:22:14,291 --> 00:22:17,336
Good thing we arrived
before this became a crime scene.

495
00:22:18,420 --> 00:22:19,963
[Fely] Hey, Cita!

496
00:22:20,047 --> 00:22:22,507
Have your husband Noel jailed!

497
00:22:23,008 --> 00:22:25,385
- What he did to you was too much.
- [sobs]

498
00:22:25,969 --> 00:22:27,596
Thank you for coming.

499
00:22:27,679 --> 00:22:29,848
[sobbing]

500
00:22:30,432 --> 00:22:33,101
Are you sure you're okay?

501
00:22:34,728 --> 00:22:36,813
[sobs] Just go back to the shop, Ame.

502
00:22:36,897 --> 00:22:38,940
No one's there.

503
00:22:40,609 --> 00:22:42,360
Um, okay.

504
00:22:42,444 --> 00:22:45,072
Just let me know
if you need anything, okay.

505
00:22:45,155 --> 00:22:48,116
[melancholic music playing]

506
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:49,201
Take care, both of you.

507
00:22:49,284 --> 00:22:51,953
- Mm, thank you.
- Take care.

508
00:22:55,665 --> 00:22:57,876
Cita, Noel is at the barangay.

509
00:22:57,959 --> 00:23:00,378
You can go face each other to file a case.

510
00:23:03,048 --> 00:23:04,257
I'll be back.

511
00:23:04,341 --> 00:23:07,511
Stay here, okay.

512
00:23:07,594 --> 00:23:09,221
[sobbing]

513
00:23:09,304 --> 00:23:11,556
- Cita, let's go now.
- [sobs]

514
00:23:12,474 --> 00:23:13,683
I'll be back.

515
00:23:13,767 --> 00:23:18,897
- [sobbing]
- [melodramatic music playing]

516
00:23:25,737 --> 00:23:26,822
[Audrey] <i>You must choose.</i>

517
00:23:28,698 --> 00:23:30,951
Your child or Ibyang.

518
00:23:42,587 --> 00:23:46,007
[melodramatic music playing]

519
00:23:46,091 --> 00:23:48,218
[Ibyang] Thank you, Tatoy.

520
00:23:49,678 --> 00:23:50,679
Why?

521
00:23:50,762 --> 00:23:55,684
[somber music playing]

522
00:23:56,434 --> 00:23:57,602
Because…

523
00:23:58,854 --> 00:24:01,857
you're still here for me.

524
00:24:02,440 --> 00:24:04,943
Sorry if…

525
00:24:05,026 --> 00:24:09,656
you and Aunt Audrey fought because of me.

526
00:24:10,866 --> 00:24:12,492
[sighs]

527
00:24:12,576 --> 00:24:13,994
Don't worry about that.

528
00:24:15,162 --> 00:24:17,289
That's how it is. Sometimes…

529
00:24:18,039 --> 00:24:22,252
you have to fight over big things,
for everyone's good.

530
00:24:22,335 --> 00:24:26,214
[gentle music playing]

531
00:24:26,298 --> 00:24:28,091
I just believe in you.

532
00:24:29,092 --> 00:24:30,260
I know you didn't do anything wrong.

533
00:24:32,220 --> 00:24:34,639
Come on. I'll take you home.

534
00:24:34,723 --> 00:24:40,228
[sentimental music playing]

535
00:24:41,479 --> 00:24:47,485
[electronic blipping]

536
00:24:51,740 --> 00:24:52,824
Are you crying?

537
00:24:52,908 --> 00:24:55,160
Your daddy is sending Ibyang home.

538
00:24:55,243 --> 00:24:56,494
[Audrey] <i>We want you to feel</i>
<i>that your daddy</i>

539
00:24:56,578 --> 00:24:59,706
<i>and I love you very much, child.</i>

540
00:24:59,789 --> 00:25:01,625
Delfin knows you're his youngest.

541
00:25:01,708 --> 00:25:02,709
[Karla] <i>What about Brother Atoy?</i>

542
00:25:02,792 --> 00:25:04,419
Did he just accept everything?

543
00:25:04,502 --> 00:25:05,629
He doesn't know.

544
00:25:05,712 --> 00:25:08,173
Brother Atoy is so kind to us.

545
00:25:08,256 --> 00:25:10,008
He needs to know the truth.

546
00:25:10,091 --> 00:25:11,509
‪UP NEXT

547
00:25:11,593 --> 00:25:12,844
- Come on, come on.
- Let's go, let's go.

548
00:25:12,928 --> 00:25:14,346
I wish…

549
00:25:14,429 --> 00:25:15,805
[sobs]

550
00:25:15,889 --> 00:25:18,558
I was really your child.

551
00:25:19,226 --> 00:25:22,020
[Ibyang] <i>So you wouldn't give me away.</i>

552
00:25:22,562 --> 00:25:23,939
[sobs]

553
00:25:24,022 --> 00:25:26,858
<i>You're the only Tatoy I have.</i>

554
00:25:26,942 --> 00:25:28,860
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

555
00:25:28,944 --> 00:25:31,905
[sobs]

556
00:25:31,988 --> 00:25:33,740
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

557
00:25:33,823 --> 00:25:35,992
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

558
00:25:36,076 --> 00:25:39,246
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

559
00:25:39,329 --> 00:25:41,248
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

560
00:25:41,331 --> 00:25:42,249
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
